dly the fact that she said there is  a high demand for her  illegal products implies that her other  customers are purchasing  said illegal products in other words  illegal  male armor finally the fact that she has  chosen to market two  male buyers in the middle of not only  the gerudo desert but gerudo  town of all places implies that her  location is  necessary because of her buyers who  logically must be located not just in  hyrule but in the gerudo desert  otherwise it makes zero sense to open a  store marketed towards men in literally  the one and only place in hyrule that  bans men  with all these clues about her customers  in mind i've speculated that there are  two possibilities for who her customers  are  the first possibility would be fellow  garuda women we can see that clearly  even though the club is pretty hush-hush  somehow gerudo women know about it and  are interested in going there  since it's more of a store than what you  would think of a club being  this implies that her customer base  could be other gerudo the natural  question is of course why they would be  interested in buying armor fit for men  tiny non-gerudo men at that well as we  know garuda women have to each leave  gerudo town to find a husband at some  point in their life  should they choose to do so of course it  could be that these gerudo women  want to purchase sets of armor or suits  of clothing for the men that they would  marry  kind of like how the princess of the  zora people will traditionally create a  suit of armor for the man she wants to  marry  i don't know why selling men's clothing  for men that wouldn't ever be  in gerudo town would be illegal and we  also don't see this happening or even  talked about at any point in the game  even when we see a garuda woman and  hylian man courting each other at the  heart-shaped lake  but still the garuda women can't be  ruled out as possible customers number  one  the second possible buyers are much more  intriguing and i'll jus